<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#north-african-elephant">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">North African elephant</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as North African forest elephant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The North African elephant was a population of elephants, now extinct, that lived in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in antiquity. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> captured and trained them as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>. They formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s military system, most famously in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibals-crossing-of-the-alps">Hannibal's crossing of the Alps</a>.</p></div>
